1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,832
Put raw bananas in a closed
box with a ripe fruit.

2
00:00:03,832 --> 00:00:05,667
The raw ones ripen faster.

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:08,933
On a dry day, a leaf shuts its tiny pores.

4
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:12,317
And some seeds sit still for
months before they sprout.

5
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:15,180
Diya tried the banana box in her kitchen.

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:18,669
She asked: what passes from
the ripe fruit to the raw ones?

7
00:00:18,669 --> 00:00:21,091
And what tells a plant to stop and wait?

8
00:00:21,441 --> 00:00:23,000
Here is the short answer.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,269
Ripe fruits give off a gas, ethylene.

10
00:00:25,269 --> 00:00:27,807
And abscisic acid is
the plant's stop signal.

11
00:00:28,307 --> 00:00:31,846
By the end, you will know the cytokinins,
ethylene and abscisic acid: how

12
00:00:31,846 --> 00:00:33,563
they were found and what they do.

13
00:00:34,213 --> 00:00:35,173
First, the cytokinins.

14
00:00:35,523 --> 00:00:36,423
F.

15
00:00:35,926 --> 00:00:39,256
Skoog and his co-workers
grew pieces of tobacco stem.

16
00:00:39,256 --> 00:00:43,746
A mass of undifferentiated cells,
called callus, grew only if auxin came

17
00:00:43,746 --> 00:00:47,823
with something extra, like yeast
extract, coconut milk or DNA.

18
00:00:48,273 --> 00:00:52,441
Skoog and Miller later found the
active substance and named it kinetin.

19
00:00:52,441 --> 00:00:56,084
It promotes cytokinesis, the
splitting of one cell into two.

20
00:00:56,534 --> 00:00:58,902
Kinetin is a modified form of adenine.

21
00:00:58,902 --> 00:01:03,271
It came from herring sperm DNA heated
under pressure, and it does not occur

22
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,589
naturally in plants.

23
00:01:04,589 --> 00:01:08,709
A natural one, zeatin, was found
in corn kernels and coconut milk.

24
00:01:09,359 --> 00:01:13,524
Natural cytokinins are made where cells
divide fast: root tips, developing

25
00:01:13,524 --> 00:01:15,286
shoot buds and young fruits.

26
00:01:15,636 --> 00:01:19,495
They help make new leaves, chloroplasts,
side shoots and adventitious shoots.

27
00:01:19,945 --> 00:01:21,899
They help overcome apical dominance.

28
00:01:21,899 --> 00:01:26,241
And they move nutrients into leaves, which
delays leaf ageing, called senescence.

29
00:01:26,891 --> 00:01:27,915
Now, ethylene.

30
00:01:27,915 --> 00:01:29,228
It is a simple gas.

31
00:01:29,578 --> 00:01:30,478
H.

32
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:30,833
H.

33
00:01:30,287 --> 00:01:34,019
Cousins found that ripe oranges gave
off something that made stored raw

34
00:01:34,019 --> 00:01:35,297
bananas ripen faster.

35
00:01:35,297 --> 00:01:37,560
Later, this was shown to be ethylene.

36
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:42,446
Ethylene is made in large amounts by
ageing tissues and ripening fruits.

37
00:01:43,096 --> 00:01:46,288
Let's follow what ethylene
does, step by step.

38
00:01:46,638 --> 00:01:47,538
One.

39
00:01:47,152 --> 00:01:51,920
In dicot seedlings, it causes horizontal
growth, a swollen axis and a hook

40
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:52,908
at the tip.

41
00:01:53,658 --> 00:01:54,558
Two.

42
00:01:54,047 --> 00:01:56,370
It makes leaves and
flowers age and fall off.

43
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,020
Three.

44
00:01:57,747 --> 00:01:59,062
It ripens fruits.

45
00:01:59,062 --> 00:02:02,113
During ripening the rate
of respiration rises.

46
00:02:02,113 --> 00:02:05,266
This rise is called the
respiratory climacteric.

47
00:02:06,016 --> 00:02:06,916
Four.

48
00:02:06,579 --> 00:02:08,798
It breaks seed and bud dormancy.

49
00:02:08,798 --> 00:02:12,754
It starts peanut seeds germinating
and potato tubers sprouting.

50
00:02:13,504 --> 00:02:14,404
Five.

51
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:18,450
In deep water rice, it makes the stem
stretch fast to keep the leaves above

52
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:19,350
water.

53
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:21,385
It also promotes roots and root hairs.

54
00:02:22,135 --> 00:02:25,543
Ethylene is the most widely
used regulator in farming.

55
00:02:25,543 --> 00:02:30,056
Its usual source is ethephon, a liquid
that plants absorb, which releases

56
00:02:30,056 --> 00:02:31,199
ethylene slowly.

57
00:02:31,649 --> 00:02:35,723
Ethephon ripens tomatoes and apples
faster, thins flowers and fruits in

58
00:02:35,723 --> 00:02:40,030
cotton, cherry and walnut, and gives
more female flowers in cucumbers.

59
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:43,235
Ethylene also starts flowering
in pineapple and mango.

60
00:02:43,885 --> 00:02:45,297
Now, abscisic acid, or ABA.

61
00:02:45,647 --> 00:02:49,698
In the mid nineteen sixties, three
teams found three inhibitors: inhibitor

62
00:02:49,698 --> 00:02:51,543
B, abscission two and dormin.

63
00:02:51,543 --> 00:02:55,066
All three turned out to be the
same chemical, abscisic acid.

64
00:02:55,516 --> 00:02:57,669
ABA is a general growth inhibitor.

65
00:02:57,669 --> 00:02:59,672
It stops seeds from germinating.

66
00:02:59,672 --> 00:03:04,125
It helps seeds develop, mature and stay
dormant, so they can survive drying

67
00:03:04,125 --> 00:03:05,025
out.

68
00:03:05,251 --> 00:03:07,728
Let's zoom into a leaf on a dry day.

69
00:03:08,078 --> 00:03:12,249
The underside of a leaf has
many tiny pores, called stomata.

70
00:03:12,749 --> 00:03:13,686
Zoom closer.

71
00:03:13,686 --> 00:03:16,625
Each stoma is a pore
between two guard cells.

72
00:03:17,125 --> 00:03:20,096
ABA makes the stomata close,
so less water escapes.

73
00:03:20,096 --> 00:03:23,828
It helps plants bear stress, so
ABA is called the stress hormone.

74
00:03:24,478 --> 00:03:26,748
Now compare ethylene and ABA on a seed.

75
00:03:27,098 --> 00:03:29,679
Ethylene breaks seed and bud dormancy.

76
00:03:29,679 --> 00:03:32,938
For example, it starts
peanut seeds germinating.

77
00:03:33,388 --> 00:03:34,698
ABA does the opposite.

78
00:03:34,698 --> 00:03:37,105
It keeps seeds dormant
and stops germination.

79
00:03:37,105 --> 00:03:39,850
In most cases, ABA works
against the gibberellins.

80
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,200
Your turn.

81
00:03:41,141 --> 00:03:42,986
A plant is short of water.

82
00:03:42,986 --> 00:03:45,208
Which regulator closes its stomata?

83
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:46,445
Pause and decide.

84
00:03:49,645 --> 00:03:50,545
ABA!

85
00:03:50,061 --> 00:03:52,075
It closes the stomata to save water.

86
00:03:52,075 --> 00:03:54,513
That is why it is called
the stress hormone.

87
00:03:55,163 --> 00:03:56,196
Remember this.

88
00:03:56,196 --> 00:03:57,327
Ethylene ripens.

89
00:03:57,327 --> 00:03:58,418
ABA says wait.

90
00:03:59,018 --> 00:04:00,647
Now, a worked example.

91
00:04:00,647 --> 00:04:02,777
Pick the regulator for each job.

92
00:04:03,127 --> 00:04:04,027
Job one.

93
00:04:03,805 --> 00:04:05,794
Keep cut leaves green for longer.

94
00:04:05,794 --> 00:04:08,223
Use a cytokinin, which delays senescence.

95
00:04:08,673 --> 00:04:09,573
Job two.

96
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,545
Ripen tomatoes faster.

97
00:04:10,545 --> 00:04:12,702
Spray ethephon, which releases ethylene.

98
00:04:13,152 --> 00:04:14,052
Job three.

99
00:04:13,895 --> 00:04:16,091
A plant in drought closes its stomata.

100
00:04:16,091 --> 00:04:17,416
That is ABA at work.

101
00:04:18,066 --> 00:04:19,527
Now, the exam trap.

102
00:04:19,877 --> 00:04:22,973
Many students think kinetin
is a natural plant hormone.

103
00:04:23,373 --> 00:04:26,261
But kinetin does not
occur naturally in plants.

104
00:04:26,261 --> 00:04:28,183
Zeatin is a natural cytokinin.

105
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:29,885
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:29,885 --> 00:04:33,075
As statement and match questions on
the uses of ethylene, ethephon, ABA

107
00:04:33,075 --> 00:04:33,975
and cytokinins.

108
00:04:34,466 --> 00:04:35,615
Exam level now.

109
00:04:35,615 --> 00:04:37,310
Read the four statements.

110
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,509
Pause and solve.

111
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:45,135
The answer is B.

112
00:04:45,135 --> 00:04:47,912
Statements one, three
and four are correct.

113
00:04:48,412 --> 00:04:50,280
Ethylene promotes female
flowers in cucumbers.

114
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:53,099
Ethephon releases ethylene slowly,
and ABA works against gibberellins.

115
00:04:53,599 --> 00:04:56,976
But ABA inhibits seed germination,
so statement two is wrong.

116
00:04:57,576 --> 00:04:59,117
Here is your recap.

117
00:04:59,117 --> 00:05:00,699
Screenshot this card.

118
00:05:03,899 --> 00:05:06,085
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

119
00:05:06,485 --> 00:05:07,385
One.

120
00:05:06,988 --> 00:05:09,305
What is the respiratory climacteric?

121
00:05:10,205 --> 00:05:11,105
Two.

122
00:05:10,572 --> 00:05:12,385
Why is ABA called the stress hormone?

123
00:05:13,285 --> 00:05:14,185
Three.

124
00:05:13,682 --> 00:05:15,147
Where are natural cytokinins made?

125
00:05:16,247 --> 00:05:20,612
Next time: how does a plant measure
the length of the night, or remember

126
00:05:20,612 --> 00:05:21,664
a cold winter?

127
00:05:21,664 --> 00:05:25,424
We find out in photoperiodism,
vernalisation and seed dormancy.
